<!DOCTYPE article PUBLIC "-//NLM//DTD Journal Archiving and Interchange DTD v2.3 20070202//EN" "archivearticle.dtd"><article xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" article-type="research-article"><?properties open_access?><front><journal-meta><journal-id journal-id-type="nlm-ta">J Cell Biol</journal-id><journal-title>The Journal of Cell Biology</journal-title><issn pub-type="ppub">0021-9525</issn><issn pub-type="epub">1540-8140</issn><publisher><publisher-name>The Rockefeller University Press</publisher-name></publisher></journal-meta><article-meta><article-id pub-id-type="pmid">5038869</article-id><article-id pub-id-type="pmc">2108848</article-id><article-categories><subj-group subj-group-type="heading"><subject>Article</subject></subj-group></article-categories><title-group><article-title>STUDIES ON ISOLATED MEMBRANES OF AZUROPHIL AND SPECIFIC GRANULES FROM RABBIT POLYMORPHONUCLEAR LEUKOCYTES</article-title></title-group><contrib-group><contrib contrib-type="author"><name><surname>Nachman</surname><given-names>Ralph</given-names></name></contrib><contrib contrib-type="author"><name><surname>Hirsch</surname><given-names>James G.</given-names></name></contrib><contrib contrib-type="author"><name><surname>Baggiolini</surname><given-names>Marco</given-names></name></contrib></contrib-group><aff id="N0x1c678d0N0x1d7ed30">From The New York Hospital-Cornell Medical Center, New York 10021, The Rockefeller University, New York 10021, and the Research Institute, Wander Limited, CH-3001 Berne, Switzerland</aff><pub-date pub-type="ppub"><day>1</day><month>7</month><year>1972</year></pub-date><volume>54</volume><issue>1</issue><fpage>133</fpage><lpage>140</lpage><history><date date-type="received"><day>25</day><month>1</month><year>1972</year></date></history><permissions><copyright-statement>Copyright &#x000a9; 1972 by The Rockefeller University Press</copyright-statement></permissions><abstract><p> Membranes were prepared from rabbit polymorphonuclear leukocyte azurophil and specific granules separated by zonal differential centrifugation. The two types of granule membranes were quite similar in ultrastructural appearance, but they showed distinct differences in cholesterol-phospholipid ratios and in protein components demonstrable in polyacrylamide gels. </p></abstract></article-meta></front></article>